{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And it sprouted</b> — at the time when it made every tree sprout from the earth, so it sprouted in the garden, and moreover, two trees within it:" "<b>And the tree of knowledge</b> — in my opinion one must add the word דעת, so it reads: ועץ הדעת דעת טוב ורע. For how can it be in construct state, when it is known from the outset? Similarly הארון הברית (Joshua 3:14), \"והנבואה עודד הנביא\" (2 Chronicles 15:8), and many like these:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {1 "The letter heh-definite article on a noun in apparent construct state is the issue; Ibn Ezra argues the noun must not truly be construct but part of a larger phrase, hence the proposed supplementation of דעת."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:48.506191124Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}